description:
Implement `useHeadlessTabs` — a headless tabs hook that produces all the ARIA attributes needed for an accessible tab interface. No styling is provided — the caller controls rendering.

**Example:**
```tsx
function Tabs() {
  const { activeTab, setActiveTab, getTabProps, getPanelProps } =
    useHeadlessTabs(['Overview', 'Details', 'Reviews']);

  return (
    <div>
      <div role="tablist">
        {['Overview', 'Details', 'Reviews'].map(tab => (
          <button key={tab} {...getTabProps(tab)}>{tab}</button>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div {...getPanelProps('Overview')}>Overview content</div>
      <div {...getPanelProps('Details')}>Details content</div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

